# 3. Structural Patterns

Structural patterns deal with object composition, creating relationships between objects to form larger structures. The Online Book Store implements the **Facade Pattern** to simplify complex subsystem interactions.

---

## 3.1 Facade Pattern

### Purpose

Provide a unified, simplified interface to a complex subsystem. Facade pattern makes the subsystem easier to use by providing a higher-level interface while hiding the complexity of interactions between multiple components.

### Problem Statement

Without a Facade, the Online Book Store system presents several challenges:

**Multiple Subsystems**:
- [UserService](file:///c:/Users/Ahmed/IdeaProjects/Online-Book-Store/src/main/java/com/example/onlinebookstore/Models/UserService.java#7-31) - Authentication and user management
- [BookService](file:///c:/Users/Ahmed/IdeaProjects/Online-Book-Store/src/main/java/com/example/onlinebookstore/Models/BookService.java#9-27) - Book operations and sorting
- [OrderService](file:///c:/Users/Ahmed/IdeaProjects/Online-Book-Store/src/main/java/com/example/onlinebookstore/Models/OrderService.java#11-134) - Order processing
- [InventoryService](file:///c:/Users/Ahmed/IdeaProjects/Online-Book-Store/src/main/java/com/example/onlinebookstore/Models/InventoryService.java#9-46) - Stock management
- [StatisticsService](file:///c:/Users/Ahmed/IdeaProjects/Online-Book-Store/src/main/java/com/example/onlinebookstore/Models/StatisticsService.java#13-153) - Sales analytics
- Multiple DAOs (`BookDAO`, `UserDAO`, `OrderDAO`, `CategoryDAO`, `ReviewDAO`)

**Complex Interactions**:
- Controllers would need to instantiate and manage all these services
- Controllers would need to understand inter-service dependencies
- Observer pattern wiring between [OrderService](file:///c:/Users/Ahmed/IdeaProjects/Online-Book-Store/src/main/java/com/example/onlinebookstore/Models/OrderService.java#11-134) and [InventoryService](file:///c:/Users/Ahmed/IdeaProjects/Online-Book-Store/src/main/java/com/example/onlinebookstore/Models/InventoryService.java#9-46)
- Session management complexity

**Example of Complexity WITHOUT Facade**:

```java
// In CustomerDashboardController
public class CustomerDashboardController {
    private UserService userService;
    private BookService bookService;
    private OrderService orderService;
    private ReviewDAO reviewDAO;
    private BookDAO bookDAO;
    private User currentUser;
    
    public void placeOrder() {
        if (currentUser instanceof Customer) {
            Customer customer = (Customer) currentUser;
            Cart cart = customer.getCart();
            
            // Validate stock
            for (Map.Entry<Integer, Integer> entry : cart.getItems().entrySet()) {
                Book book = bookDAO.getBookByID(entry.getKey());
                if (book.getStock() < entry.getValue()) {
                    showError("Insufficient stock");
                    return;
                }
            }
            
            // Place order
            orderService.placeOrder(customer, cart);
            cart.clear();
        }
    }
}
```

This is **complex, error-prone, and violates Single Responsibility**.

### Implementation

**Location**: [Models/BookStoreFacade.java](file:///c:/Users/Ahmed/IdeaProjects/Online-Book-Store/src/main/java/com/example/onlinebookstore/Models/BookStoreFacade.java)

**Responsibility**: Provides a single, unified interface for all business operations, hiding the complexity of subsystem interactions from controllers.

#### Facade Structure

```java
public class BookStoreFacade {
    // Subsystem components
    private UserService userService;
    private BookService bookService;
    private OrderService orderService;
    private InventoryService inventoryService;
    private ReviewDAO reviewDAO;
    private CategoryDAO categoryDAO;
    private BookDAO bookDAO;
    private StatisticsService statisticsService;
    
    // Session management
    private User currentLoggedInUser;
    
    public BookStoreFacade() {
        this.userService = new UserService();
        this.bookService = new BookService();
        this.orderService = new OrderService();
        this.inventoryService = new InventoryService();
        this.reviewDAO = new ReviewDAO();
        this.categoryDAO = new CategoryDAO();
        this.bookDAO = new BookDAO();
        this.statisticsService = new StatisticsService();
        
        // Wire up the Observer pattern
        this.orderService.addObserver(inventoryService);
    }
}
```

### Key Methods by Category

#### 3.1.1 User Management Methods

```java
// ==================== User Management ====================

public boolean login(String username, String password) {
    this.currentLoggedInUser = userService.login(username, password);
    return this.currentLoggedInUser != null;
}

public void logout() {
    this.currentLoggedInUser = null;
}

public User getCurrentUser() {
    return currentLoggedInUser;
}

public void registerCustomer(String username, String password, String address, String phone) {
    userService.registerCustomer(username, password, address, phone);
}

public boolean isAdmin() {
    return currentLoggedInUser instanceof Admin;
}

public boolean isCustomer() {
    return currentLoggedInUser instanceof Customer;
}

public boolean updateCurrentCustomer(String username, String password, 
                                      String address, String phone) {
    if (!(currentLoggedInUser instanceof Customer)) {
        return false;
    }
    
    Customer customer = (Customer) currentLoggedInUser;
    customer.setUsername(username);
    customer.setPassword(password);
    customer.setAddress(address);
    customer.setPhone(phone);
    
    boolean updateSucceeded = userService.updateUser(customer);
    if (updateSucceeded) {
        currentLoggedInUser = customer;
    }
    return updateSucceeded;
}
```

#### 3.1.2 Book Operations Methods

```java
// ==================== Book Browsing & Search ====================

public List<Book> getAllBooks() {
    return bookService.getBooks(null);
}

public List<Book> getBooksSortedByPrice() {
    return bookService.getBooks(new SortByPrice());
}

public List<Book> getBooksSortedByPopularity() {
    return bookService.getBooks(new SortByPopularity());
}

public List<Book> searchBooksByTitle(String title) {
    return bookDAO.searchByTitle(title);
}

public List<Book> searchBooksByAuthor(String author) {
    return bookDAO.searchByAuthor(author);
}

public List<Book> filterBooksByCategory(String category) {
    return bookDAO.filterByCategory(category);
}

public Book getBookById(int id) {
    return bookDAO.getBookByID(id);
}
```

#### 3.1.3 Cart Management Methods

```java
// ==================== Cart Management (Customer) ====================

public void addBookToCart(Book book, int quantity) {
    if (currentLoggedInUser instanceof Customer) {
        ((Customer) currentLoggedInUser).getCart().addBook(book, quantity);
    }
}

public void removeBookFromCart(Book book) {
    if (currentLoggedInUser instanceof Customer) {
        ((Customer) currentLoggedInUser).getCart().removeBook(book);
    }
}

public void updateCartQuantity(Book book, int quantity) {
    if (currentLoggedInUser instanceof Customer) {
        ((Customer) currentLoggedInUser).getCart().updateQuantity(book, quantity);
    }
}

public Cart getCustomerCart() {
    if (currentLoggedInUser instanceof Customer) {
        return ((Customer) currentLoggedInUser).getCart();
    }
    return null;
}

public void clearCart() {
    if (currentLoggedInUser instanceof Customer) {
        ((Customer) currentLoggedInUser).getCart().clear();
    }
}
```

#### 3.1.4 Order Management Methods

```java
// ==================== Order Management (Customer) ====================

public void placeOrder() {
    if (currentLoggedInUser instanceof Customer) {
        Customer customer = (Customer) currentLoggedInUser;
        orderService.placeOrder(customer, customer.getCart());
    }
}

public void cancelOrder(int orderId) {
    if (currentLoggedInUser instanceof Customer) {
        orderService.cancelOrder(orderId);
    }
}

public List<Order> getCustomerOrderHistory() {
    if (currentLoggedInUser instanceof Customer) {
        return orderService.getCustomerOrders(currentLoggedInUser.getId());
    }
    return null;
}
```

#### 3.1.5 Review Management Methods

```java
// ==================== Review Management (Customer) ====================

public void addReview(int bookId, int rating, String comment) {
    if (currentLoggedInUser instanceof Customer) {
        String reviewDate = java.time.LocalDateTime.now().toString();
        Review review = new Review(bookId, currentLoggedInUser.getId(), 
                                   rating, comment, reviewDate);
        reviewDAO.addReview(review);
    }
}

public List<Review> getBookReviews(int bookId) {
    return reviewDAO.getReviewsByBook(bookId);
}

public List<Review> getCustomerReviews() {
    if (currentLoggedInUser != null) {
        return reviewDAO.getReviewsByCustomer(currentLoggedInUser.getId());
    }
    return null;
}

public double getBookAverageRating(int bookId) {
    return reviewDAO.getAverageRating(bookId);
}
```

