### Subsystem Components

The BookStoreFacade manages and coordinates the following subsystems:

```
BookStoreFacade
├── UserService
│   ├── UserDAO
│   └── Handles: login, registration, profile updates
│
├── BookService
│   ├── BookDAO
│   └── Handles: book retrieval with sorting strategies
│
├── OrderService (Observer Subject)
│   ├── OrderDAO
│   ├── OrderItemDAO
│   └── Handles: order placement, confirmation, cancellation
│
├── InventoryService (Observer)
│   ├── BookDAO
│   └── Handles: automatic stock updates when orders confirmed
│
├── StatisticsService
│   └── Handles: revenue, sales analytics, popular items
│
├── ReviewDAO
│   └── Handles: customer reviews and ratings
│
├── CategoryDAO
│   └── Handles: category CRUD operations
│
└── BookDAO
    └── Handles: book CRUD, search, filter
```

### Usage Example: Simplified Controller

**WITH Facade (Clean)**:

```java
public class CustomerDashboardController {
    private BookStoreFacade facade;
    
    public void initialize() {
        facade = new BookStoreFacade();
        loadBooks();
    }
    
    private void loadBooks() {
        List<Book> books = facade.getAllBooks();
        displayBooks(books);
    }
    
    public void handleAddToCart(Book book) {
        facade.addBookToCart(book, 1);
        showSuccess("Added to cart");
    }
    
    public void handlePlaceOrder() {
        facade.placeOrder();
        showSuccess("Order placed successfully!");
    }
}
```

**WITHOUT Facade (Complex)**:

```java
public class CustomerDashboardController {
    private UserService userService;
    private BookService bookService;
    private OrderService orderService;
    private InventoryService inventoryService;
    private BookDAO bookDAO;
    private User currentUser;
    
    public void initialize() {
        // Initialize all services
        userService = new UserService();
        bookService = new BookService();
        orderService = new OrderService();
        inventoryService = new InventoryService();
        bookDAO = new BookDAO();
        
        // Wire observer pattern
        orderService.addObserver(inventoryService);
        
        loadBooks();
    }
    
    private void loadBooks() {
        List<Book> books = bookDAO.getAllBooks();
        displayBooks(books);
    }
    
    public void handleAddToCart(Book book) {
        if (currentUser instanceof Customer) {
            ((Customer) currentUser).getCart().addBook(book, 1);
            showSuccess("Added to cart");
        }
    }
    
    public void handlePlaceOrder() {
        if (currentUser instanceof Customer) {
            Customer customer = (Customer) currentUser;
            orderService.placeOrder(customer, customer.getCart());
            showSuccess("Order placed successfully!");
        }
    }
}
```

### Benefits

| Benefit | Description |
|---------|-------------|
| **Simplified Interface** | Controllers use one facade instead of 8+ services/DAOs |
| **Reduced Coupling** | Controllers don't depend on internal subsystem structure |
| **Centralized Logic** | Role-based access control implemented once in facade |
| **Hidden Complexity** | Observer pattern wiring hidden from controllers |
| **Easier Testing** | Can mock facade instead of multiple services |
| **Single Entry Point** | All business operations go through one well-defined interface |

### Method Categories Summary

| Category | Methods | Target User |
|----------|---------|-------------|
| **User Management** | login, logout, register, update | Both |
| **Book Browsing** | getBooks, search, filter, sort | Both |
| **Cart Management** | add, remove, update, clear | Customer |
| **Order Management** | place, cancel, view history | Customer |
| **Reviews** | add, view, average rating | Customer |
| **Book Admin** | add, update, delete books | Admin |
| **Category Admin** | add, update, delete categories | Admin |
| **Order Admin** | confirm, cancel, view all | Admin |
| **Statistics** | revenue, sales, popular items | Admin |

### Facade Pattern Flow

```
Controller
    ↓
facade.placeOrder()
    ↓
BookStoreFacade validates user is Customer
    ↓
Get customer's cart
    ↓
Call orderService.placeOrder(customer, cart)
    ↓
OrderService creates order
    ↓
OrderService notifies observers
    ↓
InventoryService updates stock (Observer pattern)
    ↓
Cart cleared
    ↓
Return to Controller
```

